WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.985
[MUSIC]

00:00:06.983 --> 00:00:10.820
&gt;&gt; There is a lot of information out there
for people applying to business school.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.134
I know I went through a lot of it.

00:00:12.134 --> 00:00:13.589
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Some of it helpful, some of it not.

00:00:13.589 --> 00:00:14.677
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH] Yeah.

00:00:14.677 --> 00:00:17.090
&gt;&gt; What are the best resources for
applying to Stanford?

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.798
&gt;&gt; And I think you make a good point,

00:00:19.798 --> 00:00:22.492
there's a lot of misinformation
out there as well.

00:00:22.492 --> 00:00:24.806
We really believe the best information,

00:00:24.806 --> 00:00:27.680
start with what we put
out there on the website.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:31.791
What's nice about it now is there's lots
of conversations with students out there,

00:00:31.791 --> 00:00:35.005
so you can learn about what it's
actually like from the students.

00:00:35.005 --> 00:00:37.327
I think that's more interesting
than hearing it from admissions.

00:00:37.327 --> 00:00:40.505
[LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; As well as there's profile information,

00:00:40.505 --> 00:00:43.160
tips about the application, start there.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.690
But one of the most important
things you can do is also go to

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:46.864
an information session.

00:00:46.864 --> 00:00:49.070
And we do about 100 of
them around the globe.

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:51.440
And the reason for
that is you'll get a panel of four,

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.600
usually three to five recent graduates.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.810
And they can tell you, we believe that
Stanford can be transformational for

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:02.180
you both in what you learn,
but also how you develop.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:04.680
So you can actually listen
to how this experience has

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.860
impacted people in their own lives,
both from how they went through,

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.140
as well as what they're doing
now when they graduate.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:13.700
So I think that's one of the best
ways you can truly be inspired, but

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.490
also get your questions answered.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:18.620
And if we're not coming to your hometown,
then go to the Web.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:19.710
We have a virtual one too,

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:23.100
where you can hear students talking and
recent alumni, about their experiences.

